    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The marginalizer is a class which is responsible for approximating the effect of a variable&apos;s error terms on the rest of the variables. This is done by approximating all error terms involving the error terms with a single gaussian prior through the schur complement. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
